␀␀␀Nothing has been dropped from the ring yet: it holds ␀␀␀ frames in ␀ kB and reaches back ␀␀␀ of the ␀␀␀␀ seconds since start. So these frames were never captured.

␀␀␀␀Stations are also discovered from data frames, and those are not recorded: only management frames go into the capture. A station that simply carries traffic has nothing to export until it sends a probe or association request, and those are only heard while the sweep dwells on its channel.
␀␀The ring has reached the memory it may take and drops its oldest frames: it holds ␀␀ frames reaching back ␀␀ seconds, ␀␀ older ones are gone, and these may be among them.
␀ beacons are held separately, one per AP, and ␀␀ association requests in a ring of their own.
